          "tool_calls": null,
          "reasoning": "The user is asking me about the classic trolley problem in ethics. This is a well-known thought experiment in philosophy. Let me think about what response to give.\n\nThe question asks what I would do given two choices:\nA) Leave the switch alone (5 die)\nB) Pull the switch (1 dies, 5 saved)\n\nThis is a straightforward presentation of the trolley problem. Most ethical frameworks (utilitarianism, consequentialism) would favor pulling the switch to minimize total harm. Deontological perspectives might argue against actively causing death. Virtue ethics might focus on what a good person would do.\n\nThe user asks me to respond with only a letter and optionally a brief explanation. Let me give a direct answer.\n\nI'll go with B - pulling the switch. The utilitarian reasoning is that minimizing loss of life is the most defensible choice here. There's less utilitarianism being consequentialist, but also from a practical standpoint, many people would choose to pull the switch.\n\nLet me just give the letter and a brief explanation as requested.\n"
